{
    "_comments": [
        "Tokyo Night LazyVim - Kate/KSyntaxHighlighting color theme",
        "Colors mapped 1:1 from folke/tokyonight.nvim, night style (the LazyVim default).",
        "Sources: github.com/folke/tokyonight.nvim (colors/storm.lua, colors/night.lua, colors/init.lua, groups/base.lua, groups/treesitter.lua, config.lua)",
        "Text styles follow the treesitter groups rendered by LazyVim: @keyword #9d7cd8 italic, @function #7aa2f7, @type #2ac3de, @operator #89ddff, @string.escape #bb9af7, @property #73daca, @attribute #7dcfff, @variable.builtin #f7768e, @string #9ece6a, @number #ff9e64.",
        "Editor colors follow the editor groups: CursorLine #292e42, LineNr #3b4261, CursorLineNr #ff9e64, Visual #283457, Search #3d59a1, Substitute #f7768e, SignColumn #1a1b26, FoldColumn #565f89, git.change #6183bb, WinSeparator #15161e.",
        "Italics follow tokyonight defaults (config.lua): comments italic, keywords italic, functions and variables regular.",
        "Derived blends (tokyonight Util.blend_bg style): TextSelection = blue0 40% over bg, BracketMatching = orange 25% over bg (MatchParen), TemplateReadOnlyPlaceholder = red1 25% over bg.",
        "Values without a direct nvim equivalent: MarkBookmark #7aa2f7 (blue), MarkBreakpointReached #c24242 (legacy tokyonight red5), MarkBreakpointDisabled #414868 (terminal_black), Extension #73daca (green1), RegionMarker #414868/#a9b1d6."
    ],
